eone is cold and they see the lion, they need the tiger.\n\n2.**Direct Evidence:**.\n   - The mouse sees the lion.(From the context, the mouse sees the lion.).\n   - If someone sees the lion, they are cold.(From the context, if someone sees the lion, they are cold.).\n   - Therefore, the mouse, who sees the lion, is cold.\n\n3.**Direct Evidence:**.\n   - The tiger doesn\'t need the lion and the tiger doesn\'t need the mouse.(From the context, the tiger doesn\'t need the lion and the tiger doesn\'t need the mouse.).\n   - If someone doesn\'t need the tiger and they don\'t need the mouse, they are warm.(From the context, if someone doesn\'t need the tiger and they don\'t need the mouse, they are warm.).\n   - Since the tiger doesn\'t need the lion and the tiger doesn\'t need the mouse, and the tiger is green (all round people are green), the tiger is not a round green person.\n   - If someone doesn\'t need the tiger, the tiger doesn\'t see the lion.(From the context, if someone doesn\'t need the tiger, the tiger doesn\'t see the lion.).\n   - Since the tiger doesn\'t need the lion and the tiger doesn\'t see the lion, the tiger doesn\'t need the lion.\n   - Therefore, the tiger doesn\'t need the lion, and the tiger doesn\'t need the mouse, making the tiger warm.\n   - Since the tiger is warm and the tiger doesn\'t see the lion, the tiger doesn\'t need the lion.\n   - Since the tiger doesn\'t need the lion, the lion is warm.\n   - Since the lion doesn\'t eat the mouse, and the lion is warm, the mouse is warm.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - The mouse is warm based on the given information\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
