yze the given statements:**.\n   - If someone eats the rabbit and the rabbit is round, then the rabbit sees the cat.(This is a conditional statement, but we need to check if the rabbit is round first.).\n   - The rabbit is round (given).\n\n3.**Determine if the rabbit is round:**.\n   - The rabbit is round (given).\nThe rabbit does not see the cat, which directly contradicts the statement "The rabbit sees the cat.".\n\nTherefore, the statement "The rabbit sees the cat" is true.\n\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
