at if Harry is nice, then Harry is not big (from the given information).\nSince Harry is not big and nice, we can conclude that Harry is not big.\nWe also know that if Harry is not big, then Harry is nice (from the given information).\nTherefore, Harry is not big and nice.\n\n5.**Check the conditions for being mean:**.\nWe know that if someone is smooth, then they are mean (from the given information).\nWe know that if someone is gentle, then they are small (from the given information).\nWe know that if Harry is small and gentle, then Harry is mean (because being small and gentle implies being smooth, and if smooth, then mean).\n\n6.**Conclusion:**.\nSince Harry is not big and nice, and we know that if someone is nice, then they are not big, and if not big and nice, then they are mean, we can conclude that Harry is mean\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
