 given directly.\n12.**Squirrel is green**: This is given directly.\n13.**Squirrel is red**: This is given directly.\n14.**Squirrel sees the bald eagle**: This is given directly.\n15.**If someone is red and they chase the bald eagle then the bald eagle is green**: This is given directly.\n16.**If someone likes the bald eagle then they like the lion**: This is given directly.\n17.**If someone is green then they see the lion**: This is given directly.\n18.**If the cow is blue then the cow likes the squirrel**: This is given directly.\n19.**If the bald eagle sees the lion then the lion sees the squirrel**: This is given directly.\n20.**If someone sees the squirrel then they are green**: This is given directly.\n21.**If someone likes the bald eagle then the bald eagle is blue**: This is given directly.\nTherefore, based on the given information, the bald eagle does not chase the lion. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
