the squirrel.**.\n12.**If something sees the lion then it sees the mouse.**.\n13.**If something is red and it visits the lion then it does not eat the cow.**.\n14.**If something is blue then it sees the lion.**.\n\nFrom the context, we know:.\n- The squirrel is red and visits the mouse.\n- The mouse is blue and red.\n- The lion does not eat the mouse.\n- The lion sees the cow.\n- The lion visits the mouse.\n- The mouse sees the lion (since the lion sees the mouse).\n\nLet\'s analyze the statement "The squirrel visits the mouse" based on the given information:.\n\n1.**Squirrel is red and visits the mouse.**.\n   - This directly states that the squirrel visits the mouse.\n\n2.**If something is red and it visits the lion then it does not eat the cow.**.\n   - This does not directly affect the squirrel\'s visit to the mouse.\n\n3.**If something sees the lion then it sees the mouse.**.\n   - This does not directly affect the squirrel\'s visit to the mouse.\nFrom the analysis, we can conclude that the squirrel is not red and does not visit the mouse.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
